      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.69,
          "end": 2.55,
          "en": "So let's see how we could use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.55,
          "end": 7.08,
          "en": "a service for data fetching because the idea behind services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.08,
          "end": 10.2,
          "en": "as you learned in this course is that you can use them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.2,
          "end": 12.903,
          "en": "for sharing data and or logic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.28,
          "end": 18.36,
          "en": "and therefore, here we can add a places service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.36,
          "end": 21,
          "en": "And actually you already have one in this project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21,
          "end": 23.28,
          "en": "but it's pretty empty, as you can tell.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.28,
          "end": 25.92,
          "en": "It got some Signal which we'll use later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.92,
          "end": 29.19,
          "en": "and it got a couple of methods here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.19,
          "end": 32.07,
          "en": "Now, what I wanna do here is I want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.07,
          "end": 37.05,
          "en": "to add another new method, which is a private method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.05,
          "end": 40.593,
          "en": "so that we can't use it from outside this service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.82,
          "end": 46.473,
          "en": "And I'll name it fetchPlaces though the name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 48.06,
          "end": 51.09,
          "en": "And now we can go to either the available,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 51.09,
          "end": 53.628,
          "en": "or the UserPlacesComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.628,
          "end": 56.73,
          "en": "and then there, grab this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.73,
          "end": 61.62,
          "en": "where we use the httpClient or where we start using it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.62,
          "end": 64.95,
          "en": "grab all that code including the pipe method up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 64.95,
          "end": 68.043,
          "en": "to excluding the subscribe method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 69.51,
          "end": 71.193,
          "en": "and cut that code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 72.96000000000001,
          "end": 74.78999999999999,
          "en": "Of course that breaks the Component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.78999999999999,
          "end": 76.49,
          "en": "but we'll take care of that later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 77.4,
          "end": 79.74,
          "en": "In the places service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.74,
          "end": 81.963,
          "en": "we can then add it here in fetchPlaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 84.27,
          "end": 85.95,
          "en": "Now, of course we must make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 85.95,
          "end": 88.53,
          "en": "that the httpClient is available here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 88.53,
          "end": 91.47,
          "en": "and thankfully that's straightforward to do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.47,
          "end": 95.31,
          "en": "because we can also inject services into services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.31,
          "end": 96.18299999999999,
          "en": "as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 97.02000000000001,
          "end": 101.253,
          "en": "So here I'll inject the httpClient into my PlacesService.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 103.68,
          "end": 106.21000000000001,
          "en": "I also have to make sure that map and catchError,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.21000000000001,
          "end": 110.00999999999999,
          "en": "and throwError are available and therefore we can go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 110.00999999999999,
          "end": 114.78,
          "en": "to available places and take those rxjs imports,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 114.78,
          "end": 119.5,
          "en": "cut them and bring them over into the places service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 122.22,
          "end": 123.063,
          "en": "like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 126.69,
          "end": 129.54,
          "en": "With that we got this fetchPlaces function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 129.54,
          "end": 133.17,
          "en": "which in the end prepares this get request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 133.17,
          "end": 136.89,
          "en": "and the pipeline for handling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 136.89,
          "end": 140.973,
          "en": "the response of that request including a potential error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 142.82999999999998,
          "end": 144,
          "en": "And my idea now is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 144,
          "end": 147.063,
          "en": "that I can use fetchPlaces in both loadAvailablePlaces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 148.32,
          "end": 150.06,
          "en": "which I plan to call from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 150.06,
          "end": 153.21,
          "en": "inside the AvailablePlacesComponent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 153.21,
          "end": 156.42000000000002,
          "en": "and loadUserPlaces, which should be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 156.42000000000002,
          "end": 158.99,
          "en": "from inside the UserPlacesComponent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 159.93,
          "end": 164.28,
          "en": "To achieve this, fetchPlaces should take the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 164.28,
          "end": 166.71,
          "en": "as an input and it should take",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 166.71,
          "end": 168.513,
          "en": "the error message as an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 169.82999999999998,
          "end": 173.223,
          "en": "and both should be of type string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 174.45,
          "end": 177.81,
          "en": "And then we can replace the hard-coded URL here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 177.81,
          "end": 180.453,
          "en": "with the URL we get as a parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 182.07,
          "end": 184.443,
          "en": "and replace the error message here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 185.52,
          "end": 187.47,
          "en": "So I'll cut that error message,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 187.47,
          "end": 190.263,
          "en": "and replace it with the error message parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 191.67,
          "end": 195.39,
          "en": "And we should then also return this produced observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 195.39,
          "end": 197.43,
          "en": "so that we can use it in the place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 197.43,
          "end": 201.06,
          "en": "where we call fetchPlaces because now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 201.06,
          "end": 202.21,
          "en": "in loadAvailablePlaces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 203.22,
          "end": 207.313,
          "en": "we can simply return this fetchPlaces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 208.23,
          "end": 209.94,
          "en": "and pass",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 209.94,
          "end": 212.32,
          "en": "the URL for the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 213.18,
          "end": 218.18,
          "en": "AvailablePlaces to it and pass the error message to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 219.69,
          "end": 221.317,
          "en": "And here that was actually,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 221.317,
          "end": 226.317,
          "en": "\"Something went wrong fetching the available places.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 228.72,
          "end": 231.51,
          "en": "So now loadAvailablePlaces is just a wrapper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 231.51,
          "end": 234.213,
          "en": "around fetchPlaces and configures this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 235.47,
          "end": 237.06,
          "en": "We can now go to the place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 237.06,
          "end": 239.88,
          "en": "where we need the AvailablePlaces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 239.88,
          "end": 242.877,
          "en": "so the AvailablePlacesComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 242.877,
          "end": 246.873,
          "en": "and there, also get rid of the httpClient call,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 248.4,
          "end": 251.583,
          "en": "and instead use our placesService here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 252.81,
          "end": 255.51,
          "en": "So instead of injecting the httpClient here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 255.51,
          "end": 257.53,
          "en": "I'll inject the placesService",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 263.64,
          "end": 264.473,
          "en": "like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 265.47,
          "end": 267.12,
          "en": "And of course you must make sure that you also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 267.12,
          "end": 271.29,
          "en": "import the placesService and we can then get rid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 271.29,
          "end": 273.573,
          "en": "of the httpClient import,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 275.37,
          "end": 277.77,
          "en": "and we can now use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 277.77,
          "end": 280.56,
          "en": "this places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 280.56,
          "end": 282.15,
          "en": "Service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 282.15,
          "end": 284.043,
          "en": "and call loadAvailablePlaces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 287.036,
          "end": 287.869,
          "en": "and loadAvailablePlaces will yield an Observable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 291.9,
          "end": 294.3,
          "en": "because it simply returns the result",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 294.3,
          "end": 298.05,
          "en": "of calling fetchPlaces, which returns this Observable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 298.05,
          "end": 300.033,
          "en": "which is created with the get method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 301.05,
          "end": 304.41,
          "en": "So therefore, in the AvailablePlacesComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 304.41,
          "end": 307.38,
          "en": "we now have much leaner code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 307.38,
          "end": 309.27,
          "en": "I still subscribe there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 309.27,
          "end": 313.2,
          "en": "I still set up that observer object here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 313.2,
          "end": 316.86,
          "en": "because whilst we could do that in the service as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 316.86,
          "end": 319.53,
          "en": "and then we could share the data to the Component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 319.53,
          "end": 321.15,
          "en": "with help of a Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 321.15,
          "end": 324.24,
          "en": "Whilst we could do that, it's often a good idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 324.24,
          "end": 327.57,
          "en": "to set up the subscription in the Component so",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 327.57,
          "end": 330.3,
          "en": "that you can also clean it up there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 330.3,
          "end": 332.97,
          "en": "in case the Component gets removed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 332.97,
          "end": 335.76,
          "en": "the service, if you would subscribe there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 335.76,
          "end": 339.57,
          "en": "wouldn't know when the Component is removed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 339.57,
          "end": 342.03,
          "en": "And it also simplifies the process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 342.03,
          "end": 344.15999999999997,
          "en": "of handling different States,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 344.15999999999997,
          "end": 346.98,
          "en": "and updating the UI based on different States",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 346.98,
          "end": 350.01,
          "en": "since it's in the Component where you wanna update",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 350.01,
          "end": 352.17,
          "en": "the UI typically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 352.17,
          "end": 355.11,
          "en": "That's why it's quite common to set up the subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 355.11,
          "end": 356.31,
          "en": "in the Component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 356.31,
          "end": 361.31,
          "en": "but have all the HTTP request configuration in a service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 361.38,
          "end": 362.943,
          "en": "as we're doing it here now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 365.19,
          "end": 368.25,
          "en": "Now, in the AvailablePlacesComponent TypeScript file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 368.25,
          "end": 372.06,
          "en": "I now also want to outsource this put request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 372.06,
          "end": 374.463,
          "en": "and therefore I'll cut this code as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 375.36,
          "end": 377.67,
          "en": "and go to the PlacesService,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 377.67,
          "end": 382.67,
          "en": "and then there I have this addPlaceToUserPlaces method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 383.31,
          "end": 386.52,
          "en": "And I'll simply return this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 386.52,
          "end": 389.88,
          "en": "which I just cut so that the put request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 389.88,
          "end": 391.89300000000003,
          "en": "is configured and sent here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 393.18,
          "end": 395.31,
          "en": "And then actually here we could even change this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 395.31,
          "end": 398.53,
          "en": "and just expect to get the placeID here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 399.75,
          "end": 402.78,
          "en": "so that we can set this as a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 402.78,
          "end": 406.353,
          "en": "maybe using the shortcut like this for this put request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 408.09000000000003,
          "end": 409.86,
          "en": "Of course, this request didn't have a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 409.86,
          "end": 411.12,
          "en": "of configuration to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 411.12,
          "end": 413.46,
          "en": "so we could have kept it in the Component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 413.46,
          "end": 416.4,
          "en": "but to have a consistent strategy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 416.4,
          "end": 421.32,
          "en": "I'll put all the HTTP request configuration in this service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 421.32,
          "end": 424.14,
          "en": "and in my Components, I'll then simply reach out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 424.14,
          "end": 427.743,
          "en": "to that service and trigger the requests from there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 428.79,
          "end": 431.94,
          "en": "In this case, by passing this selectedPlaceID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 431.94,
          "end": 434.043,
          "en": "to addPlaceToUserPlaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 435.54,
          "end": 438.63,
          "en": "By the way, something I forgot here before is that we should",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 438.63,
          "end": 441.99,
          "en": "of course also clean up this subscription here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 441.99,
          "end": 444.96,
          "en": "because this also sets up a subscription,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 444.96,
          "end": 446.31,
          "en": "so we should Store it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 446.31,
          "end": 450.33,
          "en": "and clean it up if the Component is destroyed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 450.33,
          "end": 454.38,
